cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BioBridge, please also cite SpliceAI (Jaganathan et al., Cell 2019,
  doi:10.1016/j.cell.2018.12.015), and give the BioBridge source revision recorded
  in your results CSV (column biobridge_commit).
title: BioBridge
abstract: >-
  A macOS application that runs the unmodified SpliceAI model locally on small sets
  of GRCh38 variants through a browser interface, with masked and raw scores,
  deterministic explanations and provenance-complete CSV export. Experimental
  research software; not a diagnostic.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rinatrizvanov/biobridge"
authors:
  - alias: rinatrizvanov
keywords:
  - SpliceAI
  - splicing
  - variant effect prediction
  - bioinformatics
  - macOS
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Jaganathan
        given-names: Kishore
      - name: "et al."
    title: "Predicting Splicing from Primary Sequence with Deep Learning"
    journal: Cell
    year: 2019
    volume: 176
    issue: "3"
    start: 535
    end: 548
    doi: 10.1016/j.cell.2018.12.015
  - type: software
    authors:
      - name: Illumina
    title: SpliceAI
    version: 1.3.1
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Illumina/SpliceAI"
    notes: "Run unmodified by BioBridge. Code GPLv3 as released; trained models CC BY-NC 4.0 (academic and non-commercial use)."
